[i][b]The White House Meeting Between New Westmore and USO 2028
&#8203;[/b]
2028, 01 July
&#8203;
The United States of Oceanica has recently begun to open a new proposal with New Westmore. President Krump invited President Lundy to discuss new plans to further rearrange economic agreements and establish tight security on illegal immigrants.
&#8203;
President Krump awaited the arrival of Lundy from the Neiln's Harris Military Airbase. The military airbase was opening to a wide range of news reporters gathered around the airstrip.
&#8203;
Decorated flags of both USO and New Westmore were held straight above a carp design that blends an Eagle and Fox with the added design background of a map between both nations.
&#8203;
President Krump
Be sure everything goes well.
&#8203;
Foreign Ministers
Mr. President, we will make sure this meeting goes to plan.
&#8203;
President Krump
Good
&#8203;
Security 1
They're here, sir.
&#8203;
President Krump
I want everyone to be ready on that mat.
&#8203;
A group of two F22s and four F-35s flew in a coordinated position to escort the New Westmore President Plane. The military band and a group of government officials wait at the entrance of the mat for the president's arrival.
&#8203;
15 min later, the president's plane arrived. Landing on the airstrip with an opening ceremonial welcome for the arrival of Lundy. As the plane landed to the strip of the open gathering of welcoming troops and officials, they all stood to wait for the plane doors to open.
&#8203;
President Krump shank hands with President Lundy. Then, he showed him the way to the open gathering of military bands, news reports, and officials standing from the podium.
&#8203;
USO Official
Ladies and gentlemen, please rise for the arrival of His Excellency, President Lundy of New Westmore, and the President of the United States of Oceanica, President Krump.
&#8203;
USO Official continuing*
The United States of Oceanica Military Band will now perform the national anthem of New Westmore, followed by the national anthem of the United States of Oceanica.
&#8203;
Band Commander
Band, attention!
&#8203;
Band Commander
Present arms!
&#8203;
Honor guard raises rifles up.
&#8203;
Band Commander
Play the anthem of New Westmore!
&#8203;
The military band begins playing the New Westmores anthem. All personnel stand at attention. President Lundy places his hand over his chest.
&#8203;
New Westmore Anthem:(https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UKGCQwOeE4U)
&#8203;
Band Commander
Band, ready!
&#8203;
Band Commander
Play the anthem of the United States of Oceanica!
&#8203;
The band transitions to the USO national anthem. President Krump salutes as the anthem plays. Military personnel maintain formation and salute.
&#8203;
USO anthem:(https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eCCjvSjwJwk)
&#8203;
Band Commander
Order arms!
Rifles return to their resting position in perfect standing.

President Krump
Its an honor to have the first ever New Westmore President to set foot on the USO soil. We are gathered here to show our welcome to all Westmorian. Humans or Rukati. I would like to say that Mr.President Lundy is the most handsome guy I have ever met.

I know your trip took longer to come over here, but we would like to hear your thoughts and speech about the meeting.

Clapping in the background* 
